WEBVTT

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:05.030
Thank you.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:52.820
April 6.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:56.860
Space Era 799, Imperial Year 490.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:59.810
Having learned that the Imperial fleets have scattered

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.480
various locations, Yang Wenli directed his own fleet to the Gandalfa system.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:06.940
Oh well.

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.210
I suppose a sight coming.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:09.900
Pardon?

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:11.980
The fearsome Duke Lohengrim.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:16.220
Apparently, his admirals aren't alone in leaving the Gandalfa system.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:18.260
He's headed straight for Highnessen.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:23.500
My thought was to attack once the enemy fleets were their farthest apart.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:25.310
But if we wait that long...

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.660
Odds are his main fleet will get to Heinesen.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:29.910
So in order to.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.700
To avoid that situation, our fleet will be forced to open fire on Lowengram, while his

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.520
other fleets can return without much delay.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:38.390
Is that correct, sir?

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:39.110
Correct.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:42.210
Not only must we move up the time of our planned attack,

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:45.750
but the window of opportunity we were counting on to achieve that victory

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.310
has now been drastically reduced.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.090
Plus, there'll be reinforcements.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:51.180
Hmm.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.870
Scaling down the conflict to just the two fleets was hard enough.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.330
Leveling the playing field may be impossible.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:02:59.880
Will I ever get a timeout?

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:00.960
Mm-hmm?

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.150
Requesting permission to enter.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:07.530
There hasn't been a door invented yet that I could keep you out of.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:08.710
Come on in.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.400
Sir, if you'll excuse me.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:11.390
But...

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:12.500
Yes, sir?

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:13.280
No-

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:13.930
Um.

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:15.570
Nothing that won't wait.

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:20.230
Have a seat.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.250
Sir, I'm not intruding.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:23.600
Of course not.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:25.200
So what's up, huh?

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:26.420
Why so formal?

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.820
This spreading of Duke Lonegram's forces.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.910
I wonder what you make of it, Admiral.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:34.320
You're saying there's something to be made of it?

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:37.640
Well, sir, if you'll permit me to speak freely.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:41.440
This is obviously a trap, and we're headed right into it.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:42.990
What sort of trap?

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:47.150
The enemy will no doubt be expecting us when our fleet approaches the enemy's main group.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:51.370
Their dispersing fleet would turn around and rapidly surround our fleet.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.470
We'd be captured in a giant net.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:55.020
That's the trap.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:57.920
I'm sure you're ahead of me on this.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.960
I mean, if I can figure it out...

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:03.880
Sir, are you saying that we're still going, even though it's a trap?

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:04.460
I...

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:05.290
Yes?

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:12.520
It's the younger man, isn't it, who rushes forth into action while the older sits back and urges caution.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.740
Aren't we going about this backward?

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.580
Shall I take this as a sign you're less than hopeful?

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:22.810
Try and change the subject all you like, sir, but we've still got...

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:25.560
Forgive me. You're right, as usual.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.840
There's more here than meets the eye.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:29.970
I should have known you'd be way...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:36.280
ahead of me on this sir i'm sorry look at it this way in all the time you've known me have i ever

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:42.060
consciously fought a losing battle that's right i haven't and i've no intentions of starting now

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:50.180
so you do have a plan then it's not much but yes i do it's not a chance likely to come again duke

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:55.540
lohengram is only doing what i've invited him to do even though he very well knows my intentions

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:59.360
I dropped the gauntlet, he's picking it up and returning it.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.360
At which point, you'll take the gauntlet back and match his aggression with your own, right?

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:07.720
No. Nothing so romantic as that, I'm afraid.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:14.560
If anything, romanticism will be his downfall, as I've every intention of turning his own ego against him.

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:21.020
Pride before a fall, right? I'll use whatever works. In the end, that's what matters most.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:25.600
Of course. Just remember, we need you, okay?

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:28.890
Hey, don't worry. I plan to stick around for a while.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:29.980
there's

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.200
Still a lot for me to do here.

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:32.400
Sir, I...

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:32.760
Yes?

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:37.960
It's okay, never mind.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.350
I guess that's it then.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:41.920
Carry on.

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:51.860
April 11th.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.520
Supply base on the asteroid Rudmilla.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.820
Yang's fleet completed its laying in of supplies.

