anything left undone. So that we'll have nothing left undone, huh? Half a day, whole day, what's

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:19.610
the diff? Either way, there's nothing to do. Oh, well, guess I better start looking for tonight's

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:25.300
warm body. What are you planning on doing tonight, huh? Sleeping. There you go, with your stupid

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:29.980
jokes again. I'm joking? As a joke, it's boring. As a fact,

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:36.570
it's pathetic you use jokes like others use oxygen hey I'd rather be making them

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:40.790
than be the cause of them you know what I mean a man's life can be the biggest

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:46.000
joke of all my dear Kornuff I do believe your cynical nature seems to be

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:51.360
getting the better of you it's merely the loneliness of a lonely man pay it no

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:52.740
mind my dear poplin

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:03.450
Lieutenant Commander.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:06.440
Yulian, any plans till 2400 hours?

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:09.980
Well, I thought I'd go to the mess hall. What about you?

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.870
Admiral Yang's quarters. I wonder what he wants.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:25.460
Lieutenant.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:26.220
Sir.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:28.590
Lieutenant Commander.

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:29.150
Sir?

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:38.250
Uh, Miss Greenhill.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:38.960
Sir.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:44.270
Uh, Frederica?

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:51.330
Sir, Admiral, I feel that we've finally come back to where we were 11 years ago.

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:56.030
You haven't called me by my first name since El Fasil, remember?

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:07.900
Amen.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:10.560
Uh, thank you.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:12.240
Miss Greenhill, wasn't it?

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.570
Please, it's just Frederica.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:15.940
Lieutenant, sir.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:18.540
Frederica.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:20.900
Frederica, when this battle's over,

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:24.720
I know I'm seven years older than you.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:26.040
I also-

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:26.930
I...

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:30.000
I guess I also know you're smarter than me.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.130
Really, if you think about it, I've no right to even ask you,

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:36.860
and I hope you won't think I'm pressuring you,

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:40.160
but we've got a big battle coming up,

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.980
and I know you might think it's inappropriate,

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:48.270
but I'd rather say it and regret it than regret not saying it, you know?

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:49.780
What am I saying?

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:52.370
Well, I'm not saying anything. That's what I'm saying.

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:56.150
In other words, in other words, I...

00:08:56.150 --> 00:08:57.530
Will you marry me, Frederica?

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:02.630
We'll both have our pensions

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:05.430
That should be enough to see us through our retirement.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:07.180
Also...

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:10.110
I suppose I should have mentioned this earlier, but...

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:13.630
Well, my parents were eight years apart when they married.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:15.120
If I had...

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:21.310
Is there something wrong?

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:22.800
Mmm.

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:26.390
I guess that I'm waiting.

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:27.980
for your answer.

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:32.900
The answer's yes.

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:35.210
It's yes, sir.

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:36.710
Yes, and gladly.

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:37.990
Well, that's good.

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:39.670
I, um...

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:40.810
Bye.

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:44.660
I don't know what to say. Maybe I shouldn't say anything.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:46.880
You don't say.

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:49.080
After all this time...

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:50.500
He finally found the nerve.

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:52.360
Thank you.

00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:58.420
It's basically a merry occasion.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:09:59.970
Let's toast the ham.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.500
Happy couple.

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:02.550
I, uh, already did.

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:07.130
Sir, you just said that they're getting together is a merry thing, basically.

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:08.250
What do you mean by that?

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:10.220
Of course it's marry for Yang.

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:12.380
Someone actually wants to marry him.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:13.720
And a catch at that.

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:17.790
As for Lieutenant Commander Greenhill, she may have peculiar tastes,

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:21.070
but she's marrying the one she loves, so who's to say?

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:25.180
After all, you can hold a funeral for one.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:28.000
but it takes two to make a wedding, right?

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:29.940
Then why is it just basic?

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:35.780
For the same reason, you couldn't help that first quick drink before the actual toast.

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:39.150
You've still got that crush on her, right?

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:46.920
I'm happy for both of them, okay? I am. I like and respect the both of them.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.020
And I can't say I didn't see it coming.

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:51.330
Yeah, I know. Care for another?

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:53.200
Sure, why not?

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:57.300
Julian, my boy, let an old married man give you some free advice.

00:10:57.870 --> 00:10:59.970
There's a part of people's hearts that obey...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.200
no rules and follows no logic.

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:04.400
It's not something limited to love affairs either.

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:07.240
It's kind of a system-wide thing.

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:09.680
I feel confused, even a little upset.

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:10.880
It's completely normal.

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:13.660
That's just the way the thing works. It can't be helped.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:18.270
But to be honest, I was worried that you might let this get to you.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:19.780
As a person,

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:21.020
You've a good head.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:22.540
and even better heart.

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:27.160
But when it comes to affairs of the heart, none of that matters one little bit.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:28.540
Yes, I know.

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:29.620
That's...

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:29.980
Good.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:30.880
that you understand.

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:33.600
Even if it is only in your head.

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:38.510
Now, will they still call each other admiral and lieutenant commander after marriage?

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:40.900
Of course they won't. Why would they?

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:46.650
You'd be surprised. My own wife called me Lieutenant Kazern when we were newlyweds.

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:49.440
I had to stop myself from saluting her.

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:52.440
This begs the question of us all surviving.

00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:53.500
But Julian...

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:55.360
What will you do once they're married?

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:58.290
We'd love for you to stay with us.

00:11:58.510 --> 00:11:59.470
You don't have to worry.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.440
I'm not gonna bother the newlyweds.

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:02.500
What's that saying again?

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:04.820
For a couple's privacy is important,

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:06.040
for newlyweds sacred?

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:09.030
But seriously, there's a place I've been meaning

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:10.150
to go to for a while,

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.950
which is why I'm hoping to take a trip.

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:13.270
And where's that?

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:14.520
Earth, actually.

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:15.400
Earth?

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:17.410
It wouldn't have anything to do

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:19.590
with that cult leader thing now, would it?

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.540
Doesn't really matter, does it?

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:24.020
In any event, I won't be setting out

00:12:24.020 --> 00:12:25.520
till after the ceremony's finished.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:26.630
Oh yeah?

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:28.900
To their happiness.

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:39.650
What kind of sun is that?

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:43.660
We stop Lohengram now or lose our fallback.

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:45.310
There's no other choice.

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:52.960
All 125 billion light-second space of the Vermilion system

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.760
has been divided into 10,000 partitions,

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:58.200
patrolled by 2,000 reconnaissance units.

00:12:58.500 --> 00:12:59.960
Early detection should they...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.480
therefore be possible no matter which way he enters.

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:05.240
That's the gist of your analysis, correct?

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:06.000
Right.

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:08.290
The credit for the operation, though,

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:10.430
should go to Vice Admiral Murai.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.940
I believe I know enough to leave these things to others.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:14.760
Oh?

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:18.820
I left my days of tactical micromanagement behind me

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:21.220
11 years ago when I escaped from El Fasile.

