846 heading towards sector 1227 distance from our unit is 40.6 light

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:42.960
seconds they're close sir shall we move to intercept them and what gain pray

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:47.740
tell is there to be had in downing a mere recon ship mightn't it be more

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:52.660
clever to follow them and determine the location of their main forces yes sir

00:13:58.260 --> 00:13:58.940
excellency

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:06.400
We found the enemy location. It seems we'll have enemy contact in the Vermillion system.

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:08.140
So it is there.

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:09.200
Strite.

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:11.180
Sir.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:13.380
Order the fleet to rest.

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:14.190
Sir?

00:14:15.030 --> 00:14:19.310
There'll be no immediate battle since enemy position is now known to us.

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:24.450
It's best we allow the troops to relieve tension. Three hours should be enough.

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:26.760
Drinking is to be permitted as well.

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:28.260
Yes, sir.

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:34.320
For the next three hours, rest is in effect.

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:38.340
All ships take turns with meals and getting sleep in the tank beds.

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:43.680
As we're all aware, Duke Lohengram is without rival as a tactical genius.

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:47.950
If we're foolish enough to face him head-on, we're sure to be defeated.

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:50.320
Maybe, maybe not.

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:53.730
Either you're underestimating your own ability,

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:56.370
or you're forgetting the fact that this year alone,

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:59.970
you've already taken out no less than three of the Empire's top com-

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:05.500
commanders. You forget that I was lucky. Luck isn't everything, of course, but it does help.

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:14.160
Either way, before the rest of the dispersed enemy fleets return, and the first to return will

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:20.110
likely be Wolf der Sturm, we must settle the battle conclusively. Therefore, the plan is to

00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:25.600
force our way through the enemy in tight formation and initiate quick battle. Whereas the enemy

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:29.980
objective is complete obliteration, we need but one thing. To sink their flas-

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:33.400
This, above all, will be our advantage.

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:39.210
Obviously, once the battle begins,

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:41.350
there'll be little chance to eat or sleep.

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:44.010
For that reason, I'd like everyone to rest now.

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:57.530
Well, Vice Admiral, what do you say?

00:15:58.120 --> 00:15:59.970
I'd say, how badly do you...

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:06.180
want it. I want to win more than anything with all my heart and soul. You know, next time, if you're

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:13.310
trying to convince others, you should try saying it like you mean it, Admiral, sir. Being a victory

00:16:13.310 --> 00:16:19.350
obsessed career officer is one thing, and being a garden variety opportunist who only wants power

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:26.840
is another. You, however, bear no resemblance to either of those types. If you were some hellblazing

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:29.980
demagogue type, the kind of guy who never suffers a mo-

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:37.210
doubt, I could get behind you. As it is, even in the midst of battle, I think you yourself have a

00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:46.080
hard time believing in the prevailing ideology. There's none of that once more into the breach

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:51.780
stuff with you. Yet somehow you always seem to come out a winner, don't you? Why is that?

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:57.780
Even the most miserable, impoverished democracy is better than the most benign of dictatorships.

00:16:58.210 --> 00:16:59.910
If for no other reason, that

00:16:59.910 --> 00:16:59.950
Thank you.

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:04.050
is why I fight for Jobe Trunigt against Duke Reinhard von Lohengram.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.960
Personally, I think it's a pretty good reason.

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:12.240
Rudolf, founder of the Galactic Empire, became emperor by popular acclaim.

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:16.320
Mightn't there be something similar waiting at the end of one of these...

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:18.620
What was that wonderful term you used?

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:22.040
Miserable, most impoverished democracies?

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:24.440
What makes a good democracy anyway?

00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:25.660
Or a bad one?

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:28.810
Or the most benign of dictatorships, for that matter?

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:29.780
What conditions?

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:38.530
are needed. All class one, battle alert. Distance to enemy, 84 light seconds. They're closing in

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:58.700
pretty quickly. What point is there in staying away? Enemy forces past yellow zone, now entering firing

00:17:58.700 --> 00:17:59.160
range.

00:18:00.730 --> 00:18:01.090
Fire.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:06.340
Battle of Vermillion began as any other conflict.

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:12.170
Both Reinhardt and Yang anticipated trick strategies from each other, and therefore spent considerable

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:13.750
time devising counter moves.

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:18.280
Accordingly, only the most orthodox strategies weren't first deployed.

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:25.100
However, once the actual battle began, the conflict started to spread without order, despite

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:26.960
the intentions of both commanders.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:29.960
Excellency, the front line...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:35.280
asking to be advised let each section manage on its own why else have we

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:41.060
mid-level commanders must I do everything myself so what are you reporting it to

00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:46.200
us for isn't the enemy in charge of that why don't you go ask them of course

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:50.500
communications will be intercepted dispatch messengers why else have we got

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:59.890
shuttles standing by Admiral Yang sir our flagships advance too far

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:03.920
forward. We'll only be a magnet for concentrated fire. Permission to fall back.

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:08.100
Ship level command is left to the captain. Do as you think best.

00:19:23.420 --> 00:19:26.400
Each section manage its own, eh? Fine.

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:29.770
All ships advance. Uh, sir, should we do that?

00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:32.730
We've yet to receive attack orders and, uh, well...

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:37.350
Communications are intercepted and the command system can't respond to changing situations.

00:19:37.490 --> 00:19:40.990
We may lose our chance for victory if we wait for orders.

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:43.270
The front line will take care of itself.

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:44.420
But...

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:45.220
Take a look.

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:49.200
The enemy's unable to break even the first line of defense.

00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:56.000
Rather than just sitting here, what we've got is a chance to choke the life out of Yang with our bear hat.

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:04.110
Must we fall back quite this far? It'll complicate commands.

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:04.550
Sir.

00:20:05.250 --> 00:20:06.850
The enemy's falling apart.

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:11.210
Let's move up to where I can figure things out so we don't miss our chance.

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:21.200
Devils to Nice and Thinking!

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:22.620
This is it. Fire!

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:29.970
Nice and...

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:30.920
What do you think he's doing?

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:33.420
Ternizan fleet, please come in.

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:35.870
He's quite the hero.

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:39.390
His voice may reach far, but his sight is limited.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:41.670
He's to be avoided.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:45.080
Remind me to listen to your advice next time.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:46.920
If we live through this, that is.

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:52.140
For now it would seem his ships are sorely needed to ensure our survival.

00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:55.400
Send out the shuttle and hail Ternizan.

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:04.220
And fire.

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:33.530
HOLD YOUR POSITIONS!

00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:45.520
The duty was not the purpose of their fight.

00:21:46.380 --> 00:21:50.700
However, righteousness and conviction have a way of producing bloodshed.

00:21:53.320 --> 00:21:57.640
In order to heed the call for justice demanded by the respective commanders-in-chief,

00:21:58.400 --> 00:21:59.940
it was necessary for countless...

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:05.100
soldiers to lose their lives in the fires of battle. Those in power who kept themselves

00:22:05.100 --> 00:22:09.980
back at a safe distance were often wont to insist that their righteous cause took precedence

00:22:09.980 --> 00:22:16.940
over human lives. If Duke Reinhard von Lohengram were to be accepted from the company of such

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:25.460
figures, it was because he always stood at the front lines. As for Yang Wenli, his suspicion

00:22:25.460 --> 00:22:29.970
that he had become a mass murderer was a constant one, that he was unworthy.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:35.460
to return the affections of a Frederica Greenhill and enjoy a family was caused in large part

00:22:35.460 --> 00:22:42.620
by this type of constant self-recrimination. Despite assurances to the contrary, therefore,

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:54.680
there was much yet to consider. Space Era 799, Imperial Year 490, Reinhard von Lohengram

00:22:54.680 --> 00:22:59.980
and Yang Wenli both found themselves enmeshed in an unexpected...

00:23:00.380 --> 00:23:00.840
chaotic

00:23:50.630 --> 00:23:51.310
Pops
